$[Import* std]
`!case` matches a variant with one clause per alternative, each naming its payload.
$[# area {^ {wh} {* {.w wh} {.h wh}}}]
$[# shape {^ {s} {!case s {circle r {* 3.0 {* r r}}} {rect wh {area wh}}}}]
${shape {#circle 2.0}}
expect: 12.0
${shape {#rect {. w 2.0 h 3.0}}}
expect: 6.0
A Unit payload is named too, and a clause body may itself use `!case`.
${!case {#none unit} {none u 0} {some x x}}
expect: 0
${!case {#some {#on unit}} {none u "none"} {some x {!case x {on u "on"} {off u "off"}}}}
expect: "on"
The macro's own names never capture the user's.
$[# fields 5]
${!case {#a 1} {a more {+ more fields}} {b x x}}
expect: 6
